A||||4||Cheever2||"Mail Box" shipping companies: R they OK?||||5||
Z||000000||Cheever2||05-01-2001||02:45 PM||||Getting ready to start sending out some of the stuff from my parts car (watch the Mall, I will list there soon).  The most convenient way for me to send things out would be through Mail Box Express and My Mail Box, both of which are very close to me.  LVM Safe Freight is not too far.  Everything else, like UPS etc, would be kind of a pain.  Anybody have any comment regarding the "Mail Box" type of services?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Taijiguy||05-01-2001||03:22 PM||||They're expensive. I don't know about all of them, but the one near me charges for everything. They put a piece of tape across the end of the box and charge you three bucks for packing service. A real ripoff.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||RobertVol||05-01-2001||03:25 PM||||Just make sure you keep your receipts!!!<P>I has a problem with Mail Boxes ETC.<P>I got a Quarter Window I did not need from Doug Kinney.<P>I used them to remail it. They were in the process of moving to another location. Doug sent me an e mail cause he had not received it. I checked with them and they lost it and I did not have the receipt. <P>I still threw a fit on them. Uhh they found it after saying they could not track it without the receipt. I dont think the receipt made that much of a difference when its//////////<P><BR>In the back of your FRICKIN office the whole time !!!!<P>This is probably a very rare case but the moral is KEEP you receipts!! At least you can prove the transaction was done!!||||reg||11
Z||000003||007DOUG||05-01-2001||06:22 PM||||MBE is nice because they do all the packing, and their hours are convenient, but they cost at least 30% more than using the UPS customer counter.<P>UPS just bought Mail Boxes Etc. (along with a few other companies)<P>I'm sure their service will improve.||||reg||14
Z||000004||rogergarrison||05-02-2001||11:04 AM||||their convenient, but like already said they charge almost double what reg UPS does, I try to mail stuff now Regular mail. most stuff is only a couple dollars. A personal one-I bought four wheels for the race car, and they sent wrong offset. Mail Boxes charge me $28 per wheel. I sent some other wheels with tires to someone else UPS, and they picked them up for $14 each.||||reg||1
